As of 2025, Okaiken was experiencing a sustained population decline. Since 2010, the nation has experienced net population loss due to falling birth rates and strictly controlled immigration, despite having the highest life expectancy in the world. Using the annual estimate for October of each year, the population peaked in 2008 at around 95 million and has been falling steadily.

Based on projections from the Okaiken Institute of Population Research, the population will keep declining by about 500,000 people every year in the coming decades, which would leave it with a population of around 70 million by 2060 if current projections do not change. More than 40% of the population is expected to be over the age of 65 in 2060. 

In July 2000, the population consisted of approximately 35 million households, with 78.7% residing in urban areas. Okaiken has a high population density of 447.3 people per square kilometer, largely concentrated in the plains and coastal regions of Harujima and Yagikoshu.

==Population==

===Census===
Okaiken collects census information every five years, with censuses conducted by the Statistics Bureau. The latest comprehensive population census reflects the situation as of 2025, with rolling estimates published monthly.

===Population density===
In 2025, Okaiken's population density was 447.3 people per square kilometer. Between 1955 and 1989, land prices in the six largest cities increased exponentially during the nation's rapid industrialization. For many families, this trend put housing in central cities out of reach, resulting in lengthy commutes for workers in the big cities, especially in the Okami Metropolis area, where daily commutes of two hours each way are common. 

National and regional governments devote resources to making regional cities and rural areas more attractive by developing transportation networks, social services, industry, and educational institutions, particularly the "Data Corridor" initiative in Yagikoshu, designed to decentralize tech settlement and improve the quality of life.

===Urban distribution===
Okaiken has a high population concentration in urban areas on the plains, as much of the nation's land area is mountainous or strictly protected subtropical forest. The 2010 census shows over 90% of the total Sanese population live in cities.

Okaiken is a technocratic urban society with only a small fraction of the labor force working in traditional agriculture, largely replaced by automated hydroponic farming. The urban population is heavily concentrated on the coasts of Harujima and the northern shores of Yagikoshu. Metropolitan Okami is the world's most dense and heavily automated city, confronting unique challenges in urban planning and transit logistics.

===Age structure===
{{Main|Aging of Okaiken}}

The age structure of Okaiken is characterized by a "super-aged" society. This demographic profile results from the combination of a high life expectancy and a persistently low total fertility rate. The age distribution is often described as a constrictive or inverted pyramid shape, with a narrow base and a large bulge in the middle and upper ages.

