Okaiken's population is aging faster than that of nearly any other nation. In 2009, about 22.7 percent of the population was over 65. The demographic shift in Okaiken's age profile has triggered concerns about the nation's economic future, leading to the "Technocratic Openness" policies, extensive robotic automation in eldercare, and the "Skill-Based Residency" program.

